{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuioesS9qRZtYmGzmfUB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Probably not for new code. According to the `agents@0.23.0` release notes, `subAgent()` is deprecated, along with `abortSubAgent()`, `deleteSubAgent()`, `hasSubAgent()` and `listSubAgents()`. They still work the same way, because they now call the same underlying capability as the newer API, and `SubAgentClass`/`SubAgentStub` remain as compatibility aliases. So existing code won't break, but new code should use the replacement API named in the 0.23.0 release notes. The search results didn't say what that API is called. I also only found this in a third-party mirror of the release notes, and the official sub-agents reference page still shows `this.subAgent(...)`. Check the official `cloudflare/agents` GitHub release before migrating.\n\nSources:\n- [agents@0.23.0 release notes (mirror)](https://newreleases.io/project/github/cloudflare/agents/release/agents@0.23.0)\n- [Cloudflare Agents sub-agents API reference](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/api-reference/sub-agents/index.md)\n- [Agents SDK v0.17.0 changelog](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-06-26-agents-sdk-v0.17.0/)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1090,"cache_read_input_tokens":22218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1090},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7601e32b-ebec-419a-87d5-31f24471eff1","uuid":"a64d2001-9d5a-4cab-bddc-b9bad93e142b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:14:36.980Z","request_id":"req_011CfuioedYj9oFRVa73jgky"}
